Generate bootstrap seeds or validate bootstrap runtime evidence

Usage: mantle bootstrap [OPTIONS] [PACKAGES]... [COMMAND]

Commands:
  capabilities                 Report executable and unsupported source-root operations from live host observations
  parity-report                Produce the deterministic whole-bootstrap parity gap report
  trust-report                 Verify and render the bounded source-built proof trust result
  rust-source-provider         Materialize or import a source-built Rust provider after validation
  full-source-rust-host-tools  Materialize receipt-bound Make, CMake, Python, Perl, and BusyBox evidence
  full-source-provider-admit   Bind a normalized full-source C/C++ provider to an expected BLAKE3 identity
  native-toolchain-closure     Materialize a zero-seed source-built native toolchain closure manifest
  validate                     Run build-profile preflight, build a bootstrap derivation, and save evidence
  help                         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PACKAGES]...  Packages to include (nixpkgs attribute names, ignored with --fetch) [default: bash coreutils gcc gnumake binutils]

Options:
  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose logging
      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
      --json
          Emit errors as JSON objects for tooling integration
      --store <STORE>
          Where to export final build outputs on disk. Intermediate deps stay in castore. Source inputs always come from /nix/store. If not writable, builds still succeed (outputs in castore) [default: /nix/store]
      --store-prefix <STORE_PREFIX>
          Logical store path prefix for derivation hashes. All output paths and ATerm hashes are computed against this prefix. Default: /mantle/store. Use --nix-compat for /nix/store [default: /mantle/store]
      --nix-compat
          Shorthand for --store-prefix=/nix/store. For interop testing with Nix-computed derivations
      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>
          State directory for pathinfo.redb, blobs, and logs. Default: legacy $CRUNCH_STATE_DIR or $XDG_STATE_HOME/crunch or ~/.local/state/crunch. Use --state-dir for an explicit Mantle path
      --base-store <BASE_STORES>
          Ordered list of read-only base store state directories for overlay composition. Declared in priority order (base A before base B)
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output file path, or an absent absolute provider directory in StageX mode [default: seed.ncl]
      --fetch
          Fetch the shared bootstrap seed provider instead of querying Nix. Builds the reduced normalized seed from the pinned musl.cc tarball, persists it in --store, and writes seed.ncl. No Nix required
      --source-root <SOURCE_ROOT>
          Validate a full-source root manifest and select the source-root provider path
      --stagex-lineage <STAGEX_LINEAGE>
          Materialize from one explicit absolute StageX lineage manifest
      --stagex-transition-root <STAGEX_TRANSITION_ROOT>
          Import one explicit absolute, complete protected StageX transition root
      --offline-source-preflight
          Require imported/pinned bootstrap source state before fetch-mode source acquisition
  -h, --help
          Print help
